cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  whisplab: a frame-level multi-task Transformer for automatic guitar
  tablature transcription
message: >-
  If you use this software or the accompanying case-study data, please cite
  both the software and the thesis it accompanies.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Maximilian Johannes Paul
    family-names: Voshchepynets
    email: max.developer10001@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/MaximilianJPaul/whisplab"
abstract: >-
  whisplab maps electric guitar audio to a dense tablature representation,
  jointly predicting per-string fret labels, note onsets, and eleven playing
  techniques at frame level. A multi-scale convolutional front-end over
  log-scaled Constant-Q Transform spectrograms feeds an eight-layer Pre-LN
  Transformer encoder with independent per-string heads. Trained on the GOAT
  dataset, the system reaches a note-level F1 of 0.70 on the held-out test
  split. The repository also contains the improvisation case study, in which
  the model's output is compared against a hand transcription of an
  unconstrained 26-second solo.
keywords:
  - automatic music transcription
  - guitar tablature
  - transformer
  - music information retrieval
  - deep learning
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-31"

